      "side": 1,
      "message": "`MAX_FILE_PATH_SIZE` is the sum of the following terms:\n\n1 \u003d\u003d\u003e \"/\" which is added by `file_path()` in `get_memfd_file_name()`\n6 \u003d\u003d\u003e string length of `memfd:` which is added in [1]\n249 \u003d\u003d\u003e max string length of the name provided by userspace [2]\n10 \u003d\u003d\u003e string length of ` (deleted)` \n1 \u003d\u003d\u003e NUL terminating character\n\nWhich all adds up to 267. However, the part of interest here is the name that was supplied during `memfd_create()`, which is 249, which is than ASHMEM_NAME_LEN, so the statement is true, and I don\u0027t think it is necessary to have logic to truncate the string. \n\nmemfd also enforces that the string be under 249 characters in [3]\n\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android16-6.12:common/mm/memfd.c;l\u003d369\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android16-6.12:common/mm/memfd.c;l\u003d303\n[3] https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android16-6.12:common/mm/memfd.c;l\u003d362-363",
      "parentUuid": "44ccdf1a_6a2ce397",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
